  "title": "Chapter 49: Economic Reforms in India",
  "order": 49,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pcsce10",
      "content": "Economic reforms refer to the changes introduced by the government to improve the efficiency and competitiveness of the economy. In India, major economic reforms were introduced in 1991 to overcome the severe economic crisis and promote economic growth."
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Launch Year",
          "value": "1991",
          "icon": "calendar"
        },
        {
          "label": "Core Model",
          "value": "LPG Model",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Prime Minister",
          "value": "P. V. Narasimha Rao",
          "icon": "award"
        },
        {
          "label": "Finance Minister",
          "value": "Dr. Manmohan Singh",
          "icon": "check"
        }
      ],
      "id": "o7zecd1"
    },
    {
      "id": "sonn278",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Background of Economic Reforms"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The 1991 Economic Reforms were introduced to overcome a severe Balance of Payments (BOP) crisis and high fiscal deficit.",
        "Liberalization dismantled the License Raj, drastically reducing industrial licensing requirements.",
        "Privatization promoted disinvestment in Public Sector Undertakings (PSUs) and encouraged private participation.",
        "Globalization integrated the Indian economy with the global market through FDI/FPI inflows and tariff reductions.",
        "The reforms shifted RBI's role from a strict financial regulator to a market facilitator."
      ],
      "id": "yv7wobp"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "313vkh6",
      "content": "• In 1991, India faced a severe economic crisis."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dd435pf",
      "content": "• Foreign exchange reserves were very low."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c9fna3u",
      "content": "• The government introduced economic reforms to stabilize the economy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "n78j837",
      "content": "• The reforms aimed to promote liberalization, privatization and globalization."
    },
    {
      "id": "migqjmg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Liberalization"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "p6ltyf5",
      "content": "• Liberalization refers to the removal of government restrictions on economic activities."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "26i163d",
      "content": "• It encourages private sector participation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l6ouog3",
      "content": "• It reduces government control over industries."
    },
    {
      "id": "emhms8b",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Privatization"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g7lfbma",
      "content": "• Privatization means transferring ownership of public sector enterprises to private sector."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Economic Reforms in India",
      "id": "ls8evya"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u3g2ih8",
      "content": "• It improves efficiency and productivity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "18hys4c",
      "content": "• It reduces the financial burden on the government."
    },
    {
      "id": "v7pxryk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Globalization"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vtanydr",
      "content": "• Globalization refers to the integration of the Indian economy with the world economy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pqfx43e",
      "content": "• It promotes international trade and investment."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0rfjcyy",
      "content": "• It allows foreign companies to invest in India."
    },
    {
      "id": "5czht4i",
