      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Impact of Economic Reforms"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rw0ncls",
      "content": "• Increase in economic growth."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kq41v83",
      "content": "• Growth of private sector."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lyye4a5",
      "content": "• Expansion of foreign investment."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "206q49g",
      "content": "• Improvement in technology and productivity."
    },
    {
      "id": "3lx0m27",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Challenges of Economic Reforms"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0160q3b",
      "content": "• Increase in income inequality."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "29av1qx",
      "content": "• Regional disparities."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The 1991 Economic Policy is commonly referred to as the 'Rao-Manmohan Model' of economic development.",
        "Public sector reserved industries were drastically reduced from 17 down to only 2 (Atomic Energy and Railway Operations).",
        "Full convertibility of the Indian Rupee was allowed on the Current Account in 1994."
      ],
      "id": "wjilvmt"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vtf4okv",
      "content": "• Impact on small industries."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ee9ovua",
      "content": "• Employment challenges."
    },
    {
      "id": "8g8a1ms",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SSC / SSC Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "438ra9v",
      "content": "• Economic reforms in India started in 1991."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "unp3auk",
      "content": "• The reforms are based on LPG policy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iolvf7m",
      "content": "• LPG stands for Liberalization, Privatization and Globalization."
    }
